# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# All four Dockerfiles build with the repository root as their context:
#   - backend/executor/Dockerfile        (CI docker-executor job)
#   - deploy/Dockerfile                  (gateway service)
#   - deploy/gate/Dockerfile             (gate service)
#   - deploy/executor-runner/Dockerfile  (runner sidecar, issue #106)
#
# Docker sends the entire context to the daemon before running a single
# COPY. Anything listed here is therefore exposed to the daemon even when
# no COPY references it. deploy/RUNBOOK.md notes the runner may talk to a
# remote daemon via DOCKER_HOST, so a local .env holding NEBIUS_API_KEY /
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY would otherwise cross the wire during `compose build`.
# AGENTS.md forbids secrets in the repository or logs; this keeps them out
# of the build context too.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore. Every COPY path in the four Dockerfiles stays
# reachable: backend/, frontend/, demo/scenarios/, scripts/seed_demo.py,
# deploy/, and backend/requirements.lock.
# scripts/check_dockerignore.py asserts both properties.

# Credentials and local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# VCS metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.codex
.gemini
.agents

# Dependencies and generated output
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
dist/
build/
.next/
coverage/
.pytest_cache/

# Private runtime artifacts
traces/
logs/
*.log
runtime-data/
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Local editor and OS state
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Not needed inside any image (docs, spikes, local scratch)
docs/
poc/
*.md